# TURKEY BURGERS
## info  
* About 10 minutes prep, 15 minutes total
* about 4 servings  

## ingredients
* 1 ¼ pounds 93% lean ground turkey
* ½ cup whole-milk ricotta cheese
* ½ teaspoon salt
* ½ teaspoon ground black pepper
* 2 teaspoons Worcestershire sauce
* 2 teaspoons Dijon mustard
* 1 tablespoon vegetable or canola oil
* 4 hamburger buns and preferred toppings

## steps  
1. Mix ricotta, salt, pepper, Worcestershire sauce, and Dijon mustard gently in a bowl. Once fully combined, add turkey and recombine.
1. Shape the mix into four equal patties, pressing a slight dimple into the center of each.
1. Heat oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.
1. Cook patties without moving them until a dark golden crust forms, about 3 to 4 minutes.
1. Flip the burgers, cook until done through, and transfer to buns with your favorite toppings.

## notes  
* Adding whole-milk ricotta to the meat keeps lean turkey moist and tender.

